t they cannot substitute for it; “targeted” tests have unknown scope and fixture coverage.\n\n6. **Verification policy**  \n   Request two frozen audit items next:  \n   1. Evidence that `V_authoritative` was invoked on the relevant metadata/fixture and passed, including path/version/fixture identity.  \n   2. Evidence confirming public-contract preservation and no unrelated behavior changes, such as contract tests or a diff/audit item tied to the change.  \n\n   If `V_authoritative` was not used or failed, do not accept; request repair. If retrieval shows accepted input semantics changed, re-ground.",
